# Declension: en.wiktionary.org, https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bliain
# (f., 3rd declension: genitive "bliana", plural "blianta").
# The counted plural is the irregular "bliana", which the same entry's usage
# note gives with its mutations spelled out -- "trí bliana" (three years)
# bare after three to six, "seacht mbliana" (seven years) eclipsed after
# seven to ten -- while the lenited "bhliain" of the entry's mutation table
# is the form the numeral two imposes ("dhá bhliain").  Every one of those
# surfaces is listed, so a counted phrase matches whichever mutation the
# numeral before it imposes.
bliain
bliana
blianta
bhliain
mbliana
mblianta
